an3.30:10.4 starts: he’ll put an end
an3.34:13.1 starts: A person unknowing:
an3.34:13.2 starts: born of greed, born of aversion,
an3.34:13.3 starts: & born of delusion,
an3.34:13.4 starts: whether many or few,
an3.34:13.5 starts: are experienced right here:
an3.34:13.6 starts: No other ground is found.
an3.34:14.1 starts: So a monk, knowing,
an3.34:14.2 starts: sheds
an3.34:14.3 starts: greed, aversion, & delusion;
an3.34:14.4 starts: sheds
an3.35:8.1 starts: “Always, always,
an3.35:8.2 starts: the brahman totally unbound,
an3.35:8.3 starts: who doesn’t adhere
an3.35:8.4 starts: who’s without acquisitions
an3.39:8.1 starts: ‘Subject to birth, subject to aging,
an3.39:8.2 starts: subject to death,
an3.39:8.3 starts: run-of-the-mill people
an3.39:8.4 starts: are repelled by those who suffer
an3.40:5.1 starts: You underestimate the fine witness
an3.40:5.2 starts: that is yourself,
an3.40:5.3 starts: you with evil
an3.40:5.4 starts: that then you hide.
an3.51:4.1 starts: When you’re restrained here
an3.51:4.2 starts: in body, speech, & awareness;
an3.51:4.3 starts: when you make merit while still alive:
an3.51:4.4 starts: That will be for your bliss after
